Below is a “cook‑book” style walk‑through for building a tiny JSON‑API in **Rust** using **Axum** *or* **Actix‑Web**.  
I’ll cover the essentials once for each framework, so you can pick the one that fits your taste.

> **TL;DR**  
> - Add the crate to `Cargo.toml`.  
> - Define your data structures (`serde::Serialize`, `Deserialize`).  
> - Create async request handlers.  
> - Wire them up to a router and run the server.  
> - Hit the endpoints with `curl` or Postman.  

Below, the two sections are completely independent – copy the one you like and ignore the other.

---

## 1. Axum – The “Tower‑based” Way

### 1.1 Why Axum?

- Built on top of **Tower** – gives you ready‑made middleware (logging, auth, CORS).  
- Zero‑copy request/response handling.  
- Works nicely with `tokio`, `hyper`, and the `async‑std` ecosystem.  

### 1.2 Setup

```bash
# new project
cargo new axum-demo
cd axum-demo
```

`Cargo.toml`

```toml
[package]
name = "axum-demo"
version = "0.1.0"
edition = "2021"

[dependencies]
axum = "0.6"          # latest stable
tokio = { version = "1", features = ["full"] }
serde = { version = "1", features = ["derive"] }
serde_json = "1"
tower-http = { version = "0.4", features = ["cors"] }
```

> **Tip**: Use `cargo add axum tokio serde serde_json tower-http` if you have the Cargo add helper.

### 1.3 Basic Data Types

```rust
// src/main.rs
use serde::{Deserialize, Serialize};

#[derive(Serialize, Deserialize, Debug)]
struct Todo {
    id: u32,
    title: String,
    completed: bool,
}
```

### 1.4 Handlers

Axum handlers can be normal async functions that return any type that implements `IntoResponse`.  
We’ll use the convenient `Json<T>` extractor/response type.

```rust
use axum::{
    extract::{Extension, Json, Path},
    response::IntoResponse,
    routing::{get, post, put},
    Router,
};
use std::sync::{Arc, Mutex};

type TodoDb = Arc<Mutex<Vec<Todo>>>;

// GET /todos
async fn list_todos(db: Extension<TodoDb>) -> Json<Vec<Todo>> {
    let todos = db.lock().unwrap();
    Json(todos.clone())
}

// GET /todos/:id
async fn get_todo(
    Path(id): Path<u32>,
    Extension(db): Extension<TodoDb>,
) -> Result<Json<Todo>, (StatusCode, String)> {
    let todos = db.lock().unwrap();
    match todos.iter().find(|t| t.id == id) {
        Some(todo) => Ok(Json(todo.clone())),
        None => Err((StatusCode::NOT_FOUND, format!("Todo {} not found", id))),
    }
}

// POST /todos
async fn create_todo(
    Json(payload): Json<Todo>,
    Extension(db): Extension<TodoDb>,
) -> (StatusCode, Json<Todo>) {
    let mut todos = db.lock().unwrap();
    let mut new_todo = payload;
    // Very naive ID assignment
    new_todo.id = todos.iter().map(|t| t.id).max().unwrap_or(0) + 1;
    todos.push(new_todo.clone());
    (StatusCode::CREATED, Json(new_todo))
}

// PUT /todos/:id
async fn update_todo(
    Path(id): Path<u32>,
    Json(payload): Json<Todo>,
    Extension(db): Extension<TodoDb>,
) -> Result<Json<Todo>, (StatusCode, String)> {
    let mut todos = db.lock().unwrap();
    match todos.iter_mut().find(|t| t.id == id) {
        Some(todo) => {
            todo.title = payload.title;
            todo.completed = payload.completed;
            Ok(Json(todo.clone()))
        }
        None => Err((StatusCode::NOT_FOUND, format!("Todo {} not found", id))),
    }
}
```

### 1.5 Build the Router

```rust
#[tokio::main]
async fn main() {
    // Simple in‑memory DB
    let db: TodoDb = Arc::new(Mutex::new(vec![
        Todo { id: 1, title: "Learn Rust".into(), completed: false },
        Todo { id: 2, title: "Write API".into(), completed: false },
    ]));

    let app = Router::new()
        .route("/todos", get(list_todos).post(create_todo))
        .route("/todos/:id", get(get_todo).put(update_todo))
        .layer(Extension(db))
        .layer(tower_http::cors::CorsLayer::new());

    // 127.0.0.1:3000
    axum::Server::bind(&"0.0.0.0:3000".parse().unwrap())
        .serve(app.into_make_service())
        .await
        .unwrap();
}
```

### 1.6 Run & Test

```bash
cargo run
```

```
$ curl http://localhost:3000/todos
[{"id":1,"title":"Learn Rust","completed":false},{"id":2,"title":"Write API","completed":false}]
```

```
$ curl -X POST -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
      -d '{"title":"Learn Axum","completed":false}' \
      http://localhost:3000/todos
{"id":3,"title":"Learn Axum","completed":false}
```

