## 2. Actix‑Web – The “Actor‑based” Classic

### 2.1 Why Actix‑Web?

- Mature, battle‑tested, and fast.  
- Offers a rich middleware stack (session, compression, etc.).  
- The “actor” model is optional; you can write pure async code just like Axum.  

### 2.2 Setup

```bash
cargo new actix-demo
cd actix-demo
```

`Cargo.toml`

```toml
[package]
name = "actix-demo"
version = "0.1.0"
edition = "2021"

[dependencies]
actix-web = "4"
serde = { version = "1", features = ["derive"] }
serde_json = "1"
tokio = { version = "1", features = ["full"] }
```

### 2.3 Data Types & DB

```rust
// src/main.rs
use serde::{Deserialize, Serialize};
use std::sync::{Arc, Mutex};

#[derive(Serialize, Deserialize, Clone)]
struct Todo {
    id: u32,
    title: String,
    completed: bool,
}

type TodoDb = Arc<Mutex<Vec<Todo>>>;
```

### 2.4 Handlers

Actix‑Web uses the `web::Json<T>` extractor and the `HttpResponse` builder.

```rust
use actix_web::{get, post, put, web, App, HttpResponse, HttpServer, Responder};

#[get("/todos")]
async fn list_todos(db: web::Data<TodoDb>) -> impl Responder {
    let todos = db.lock().unwrap();
    HttpResponse::Ok().json(todos.clone())
}

#[get("/todos/{id}")]
async fn get_todo(
    path: web::Path<u32>,
    db: web::Data<TodoDb>,
) -> Result<impl Responder, actix_web::Error> {
    let id = path.into_inner();
    let todos = db.lock().unwrap();
    if let Some(todo) = todos.iter().find(|t| t.id == id) {
        Ok(HttpResponse::Ok().json(todo.clone()))
    } else {
        Ok(HttpResponse::NotFound().body(format!("Todo {} not found", id)))
    }
}

#[post("/todos")]
async fn create_todo(
    payload: web::Json<Todo>,
    db: web::Data<TodoDb>,
) -> impl Responder {
    let mut todos = db.lock().unwrap();
    let mut new_todo = payload.into_inner();
    new_todo.id = todos.iter().map(|t| t.id).max().unwrap_or(0) + 1;
    todos.push(new_todo.clone());
    HttpResponse::Created().json(new_todo)
}

#[put("/todos/{id}")]
async fn update_todo(
    path: web::Path<u32>,
    payload: web::Json<Todo>,
    db: web::Data<TodoDb>,
) -> impl Responder {
    let id = path.into_inner();
    let mut todos = db.lock().unwrap();
    match todos.iter_mut().find(|t| t.id == id) {
        Some(todo) => {
            todo.title = payload.title.clone();
            todo.completed = payload.completed;
            HttpResponse::Ok().json(todo.clone())
        }
        None => HttpResponse::NotFound().body(format!("Todo {} not found", id)),
    }
}
```

### 2.5 Build & Run

```rust
#[actix_web::main]
async fn main() -> std::io::Result<()> {
    let db: TodoDb = Arc::new(Mutex::new(vec![
        Todo { id: 1, title: "Learn Actix".into(), completed: false },
        Todo { id: 2, title: "Write API".into(), completed: false },
    ]));

    HttpServer::new(move || {
        App::new()
            .app_data(web::Data::new(db.clone()))
            .service(list_todos)
            .service(get_todo)
            .service(create_todo)
            .service(update_todo)
    })
    .bind(("127.0.0.1", 8080))?
    .run()
    .await
}
```

### 2.6 Test

```bash
cargo run
```

```
$ curl http://127.0.0.1:8080/todos
[{"id":1,"title":"Learn Actix","completed":false},{"id":2,"title":"Write API","completed":false}]
```

```
$ curl -X POST -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
      -d '{"title":"Learn Actix Web","completed":false}' \
      http://127.0.0.1:8080/todos
{"id":3,"title":"Learn Actix Web","completed":false}
```

